quran[27]{c,v,t}:
  55,41,"The evildoers will be recognized by the darkness of their faces and so they will be pulled, seized by their forelocks and feet."
  55,42,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,43,(It will be said to them:) ‘It is this Hell which the evildoers used to deny.’
  55,44,They will move about in that (Hell) and in the boiling hot water.
  55,45,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,46,"And whoever fears standing before his Lord (for meeting), for him are two Gardens."
  55,47,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,48,They are (green and fresh Gardens) with deep thick branches.
  55,49,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,50,Two springs are flowing in both of them.
  55,51,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,52,In them are two kinds of every fruit.
  55,53,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,54,"The residents of Paradise will be reclining on couches lined with fine and thick brocade (i.e., satin) and the fruits of both the Gardens will be hanging low (over them)."
  55,55,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,56,"And in them will be (chaste maidens) with downcast gazes, untouched either by any man or jinn."
  55,57,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,58,As if they (chaste maidens) were rubies and pearls.
  55,59,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,60,The reward of good cannot be anything but good.
  55,61,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,62,And apart from these two there are also two more gardens (for them).
  55,63,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,64,Both appear deep green tinting black.
  55,65,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
  55,66,There are two springs which will be gushing with force in these two (as well).
  55,67,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
